As a personal idiosyncracy, when I #Name a class of objects, I
always use initial caps.

So I'll #name a whistle "Tin" or "Magic", a lamp "Magic", "Oil"
or "Lamp 1", a gem "Soft Red 1", etc.

The practice is of essentially no value except in allowing you to
quickly see which inventory items have not yet been formally
identified.  This, in turn, is of benefit primarily when sorting
items in preparation for a lucky roll on a blessed scroll of identify.

